comments[18]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-29T16:56:18.859Z","harness:claude-code","Measured behaviour of the ad-hoc reopen path, sandbox tracker, build 2026.7.29.\n\nClosing an item then running update --status in_progress succeeds with exit 0 and changed_field_count 4. Reading the item afterwards: close_reason null, closed_at null, resolution null. All three closure fields are erased in place, not superseded, so the item's own record no longer says it was ever closed or why. The prior closure survives only inside the history stream, which means the answer to \"has this recurred, and how many times\" is reachable only by replaying every stream.\n\nThis is consistent with the third criterion here - terminal fields that must not survive are cleared by the existing update path - and it sharpens the second one. The prior closure entry does remain in history, so the criterion is satisfiable, but nothing on the item points at it and no op distinguishes a reopen from an ordinary status edit, so a reader cannot tell a reopened item from one that was never closed without a replay.\n\nTwo consequences worth carrying into the implementation. A reopen wants its own op in the history vocabulary, which places it inside pm-0elqjj's enumeration rather than reusing update. And recurrence rate becomes a measurable quality signal for the first time once the transition is distinguishable, which is a downstream consumer for the flow-metrics work rather than a criterion here.\n\nRelated probe on the same path: closed to draft also succeeds, moving a terminal item into the provisional tier tracked by pm-xpzped.\n"
  "2026-08-19T16:37:14.746Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-19: selected after a complete all-status 2,524-item inventory (2,190 closed, 320 open, 14 canceled), focused duplicate searches, full live metadata/comments/history/relationship reads, and GitHub issue lineage verification. This item is actively edited in one coupled SDK-first recurrence and executable-guidance PR spanning lifecycle primitives, CLI/MCP contracts, immutable history, capability-aware hints, generated agent guidance, recovery assurance, docs, exact coverage, and temporary installed-consumer acceptance. Unrelated backlog items remain open and unclaimed."
  "2026-08-19T16:44:23.515Z","harness:codex","TDD red evidence: focused recurrence suite fails because the SDK lifecycle/reopen module is intentionally absent before implementation."
  "2026-08-19T18:27:28.535Z","harness:codex","Evidence: implemented an atomic noun-first recurrence lifecycle across CLI, SDK, generic action dispatch, and MCP.  requires a reason, accepts only closed/canceled targets, clears active terminal fields, preserves prior closure evidence in immutable structured history, and emits a compact recurrence receipt. Manual temporary-project acceptance validated init guidance, create, close, reopen, full get, and full history. Focused linked test passed 6/6; integration and complete repository coverage passed; exact coverage is 100/100/100/100 across 534 files and 7,618 tests."
  "2026-08-19T18:28:16.757Z","harness:codex","Correction to prior evidence entry: the public command is pm item reopen ID REASON. It requires a reason, accepts only closed or canceled targets, clears active terminal fields, preserves prior closure evidence in structured immutable history, and emits a compact recurrence receipt. Manual temporary-project acceptance and the linked 6-test suite passed; full coverage is 100/100/100/100 across 534 files and 7,618 tests."
  "2026-08-19T18:49:19.593Z","harness:codex","Token-efficiency evidence: release preflight initially measured commands.item at 670 bytes against the existing 568-byte ceiling. Compressed parent and subcommand descriptions without removing capability; the unchanged 112-surface token gate now passes under the existing baseline, so recurrence did not require a budget increase."
  "2026-08-19T19:19:00.445Z","harness:codex","Review evidence: manual adapter review removed an unnecessary never assertion from the extracted MCP close dispatcher. Typecheck and the 31-test focused CLI, action-parity, reopen unit, and reopen integration suite pass after the cleanup."
  "2026-08-19T19:20:08.130Z","harness:codex","Pull request evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1063 carries the reviewed SDK, CLI, MCP, contract, documentation, test, changelog, and tracker delivery at exact head 1d85f3a0d."
  "2026-08-19T20:12:31.814Z","harness:codex","Review remediation evidence: CodeRabbit exact-head findings drove complete CLI exposure for item reopen, runtime flag registration, public core SDK exports, immutable previous-terminal history receipts, fail-closed receipt validation, and transport force propagation. Generic runAction integration now proves the same recurrence envelope as the typed SDK. Focused tests pass 15 of 15; full coverage passes 100/100/100/100 across 534 files and 7,619 tests. Manual temporary-project acceptance passed create, close, reopen, get, and history with prior resolution retained only in immutable recurrence evidence."
  "2026-08-19T20:32:04.407Z","harness:codex","Exact-head CI remediation: the public mutateItem compatibility overload now documents both its public signature and implementation entrypoint. The authoritative static-quality gate reports 100% source, exported, and member docstring coverage (4,204/4,204 exports), with zero violations; ESLint passes. The complete static chain passed repository assurance, package boundaries, SDK parity, grammar, flag, token, refusal, tracker-context, graph, record-integrity, and SDK import-cost gates. Its unrelated host-timing probe varied between get +3 ms and claim +16 ms while hosted performance checks remained green; no benchmark ceiling or runtime behavior was changed."
  "2026-08-19T21:22:29.229Z","harness:codex","Final review-remediation evidence: resolved every actionable exact-head recurrence finding by propagating global author overrides, resolving structured history context before any item write, normalizing direct SDK receipt statuses, exporting PreviousTerminalEvidence through ./sdk, ./sdk/core, and ./sdk/runtime, bounding compact recurrence reason and prior terminal text to 256 characters, and generating the executable noun-first 'item reopen' recovery command. Rejection and resolver-failure tests prove item and history atomicity. Focused suite passed 52/52; repository static assurance passed; full coverage passed 534/534 files and 7,622/7,622 tests at exact 100/100/100/100. Manual /tmp/tmp.UQRSqSQdaN acceptance passed create, close, global-author reopen, full get, and full immutable history checks."
  "2026-08-19T21:25:49.190Z","harness:codex","Final tracker-integrity evidence: pm validate --check-resolution --check-history-drift --check-storage-integrity --counts scanned 2,524 items and 2,539 history streams with zero hash, chain, workspace-state, storage, or merge-fence failures. The 295 resolution warnings are the unchanged pre-existing repository baseline; all three delivered items now carry complete resolution, expected-result, actual-result, and close-reason metadata. pm list --status in_progress reports zero items."
  "2026-08-19T22:46:20.579Z","harness:codex","Post-merge evidence: PR #1063 merged to main as f4cbd5fd39a8a4caf4f0ec6b7cdbadc275a7dd75. Merged-main CI 32305957443, CodeQL 32305956812, Security 32305956810, Docs 32305956817, Scorecard 32305956983, and CodSpeed 32305956875 all passed. Existing same-day release v2026.8.19 remained unique; npm latest, npx, and bunx all resolved 2026.8.19. Required Sentry/telemetry gate passed with 0 critical and 0 high issues in 14 days, 2.38 percent finish error rate, and 0 failures missing error codes. Explicit telemetry flush drained 1 to 0 with queue_progressed true and queue_empty true."
  "2026-09-01T04:31:17.765Z","harness:codex","Review extension evidence: Cubic comments 3900531662 and 3900765326 exposed that the generic pm update terminal-to-active path cleared timestamps and close_reason but retained structured outcome fields and fixed_version. The canonical SDK update pipeline now clears the complete terminal evidence set; explicit pm item reopen continues to preserve prior closure inside its immutable recurrence receipt."
  "2026-09-01T04:33:35.181Z","harness:codex","Terminal extension evidence: the canonical recurrence unit cohort passes 9 tests and the generic/explicit lifecycle parity cohort passes 122 tests. Generic update now clears closed_at, completed_at, close_reason, resolution, expected_result, actual_result, and fixed_version on every terminal-to-active transition while immutable history retains prior closure evidence."
  "2026-09-01T06:45:42.208Z","harness:codex","Review-source correction: CodeRabbit identified that the generated changelog faithfully rendered this item's pre-implementation problem title as a current supported-behavior claim. Updated the canonical PM title to the delivered positive contract; CHANGELOG.md remains generator-owned and will be refreshed only through the latest pm-changelog package."
  "2026-09-01T06:46:35.874Z","harness:codex","Generated changelog verification: pm-changelog 2026.8.31 installed and changelog generation/check passed. Because all three actively edited canonical owners remain in_progress, their entries are correctly absent until structured closure; generation will be repeated after close so the corrected positive recurrence title appears in Unreleased."
  "2026-09-01T06:57:19.807Z","harness:codex","Post-close generated evidence: pm-changelog 2026.8.31 now emits 'GH-796: duplicate recurrence now reopens the canonical terminal item instead of creating a second item' under Unreleased/Added with the main-branch .toon link; changelog check reports unchanged."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-19T18:27:29.126Z","harness:codex","A recurrence primitive must be a first-class atomic transition: preserving previous terminal evidence in the reopen history context is safer and more useful than asking callers to reconstruct recurrence from separate reads and updates."
